artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let $k$ be a field and consider the standard graded polynomial ring $S_n = k[x_1,\dots,x_n]$. For a homogeneous ideal $I \subseteq S_n$, let $\operatorname{reg}(I)$ denote the Castelnuovo–Mumford regularity of $I$ (the smallest integer $r$ such that for every $i$, every minimal $i$-th syzygy of $I$ sits in degree at most $r+i$), and let $d(I)$ denote the largest degree appearing among a minimal homogeneous system of generators of $I$.

Fix a constant $D \geq 2$. Construct three explicit families of homogeneous ideals $\{I_n\}_{n\geq n_0}$, with $I_n \subseteq S_n$ and $d(I_n) \leq D$ for all $n$, such that:

(a) $\operatorname{reg}(I_n)$ grows polynomially in $n$ (i.e., $\operatorname{reg}(I_n) = \Theta(n^c)$ for some $c \geq 1$);

(b) $\operatorname{reg}(I_n)$ grows singly exponentially in $n$ (i.e., $\operatorname{reg}(I_n) = \Theta(a^n)$ for some $a>1$);

(c) $\operatorname{reg}(I_n)$ grows doubly exponentially in $n$ (i.e., $\operatorname{reg}(I_n) \geq 2^{2^{\,cn}}$ for some $c>0$ and sufficiently large $n$).

In each case the maximal degree $D$ of the generators must remain fixed independently of $n$.

